---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout title="Now · Puffs of Smoke" description="What Jon Kohlmeier is focused on right now.">
  <header class="page-header container-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Now</p>
    <h1>A snapshot of what has my attention.</h1>
    <p class="page-header__lede">
      This page is a periodic record of the work, questions, and small pleasures occupying my days.
    </p>
    <p class="page-updated">Last updated November 2025</p>
  </header>

  <div class="now-grid container-page">
    <section>
      <p class="section-number">01</p>
      <h2>Working on</h2>
      <p>
        Crafting a more delightful customer experience: refining email templates, refreshing web pages, improving
        response times, and simplifying the processes behind them so front-line associates can focus on serving people.
      </p>
      <p>
        I’m also rebuilding lead flows from top of funnel to close, cleaning up data, and connecting teams around clearer
        language and better shared systems.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">02</p>
      <h2>Reading & learning</h2>
      <p>
        I’m spending time in HubSpot betas, talking with product teams, and exploring AI-assisted coding. I keep coming
        back to the craft of Revenue Operations, the human side of automation, and the idea that leadership is something
        you practice rather than something you collect from a podcast.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">03</p>
      <h2>Enjoying</h2>
      <p>
        Cool fall weather, walks with the dog, leaves underfoot, and reading <em>Blueberries for Sal</em> to my daughter.
        I’m between wine fermentations, but still enjoying a pipe and a glass of wine most evenings—and conversations on
        <a href="https://twistoflemonpod.com">Life with a Twist of Lemon</a> with Stan.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <p class="section-number">04</p>
      <h2>Thinking about</h2>
      <p>
        Rebuilding the writing habit, making room for reflection and creative work, and being more intentional with time,
        money, and energy. I’m especially interested in systems that fade into the background and leave people more room
        to do the work that matters.
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</SiteLayout>
